       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it would be a serious overdose.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day. The maximum for an adult is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 3000 mg is three times the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** Even with normal liver function, 9 g/day could cause acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure. At 70 kg, an acute ingestion above about 150 mg/kg (about 10.5 g) is treated as a potential toxic exposure, and this order would put the patient close to that every day.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours**, not to exceed 3\u20134 g/day\n\nIf you really do want 3000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
